{{also|re-collection}}
==English==

===Etymology 1===
Via {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|récollection|lang=fr}} or the verb {{term|recollect}}, both from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|recollectus|lang=la}}, the past participle of {{term|recolligere||to collect again|lang=la}}, itself from {{term|re-|lang=la}} + {{term|colligere||to gather|lang=la}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/ɹɛkəˈlɛkʃən/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɛkʃən|lang=en}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# The act of recollecting, or [[recall]]ing to the memory; the operation by which objects are recalled to the memory, or ideas revived in the mind; reminiscence; remembrance.
# The power of recalling ideas to the mind, or the period within which things can be recollected; remembrance
#: ''Alas that distant event isn't within my '''recollection''' anymore.
# That which is recollected; something called to mind; a [[reminiscence]].
#: ''One of his earliest '''recollections'''." - {{w|Thomas Babington Macaulay}}.
# {{context|archaic|lang=en}} (also spelled [[re-collection]]) The act or practice of collecting or concentrating the mind; [[concentration]]; [[self-control]].
#: ''From such an education Charles contracted habits of gravity and '''recollection'''.
# {{context|Philippines|lang=en}} A spiritual [[retreat]].

